  "verbalization": "Jatamanin C is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and a complex metabolite. These compounds are both implicated in targeting prostate cells, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of pathways that affect prostate cell function. The evidence indicates that Jatamanin C may interact with SNU-387, which in turn affects prostate cells through a series of molecular interactions. The presence of multiple targets and their shared effect on prostate cells suggests a possible role in regulating cellular processes critical to prostate health. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Jatamanin C could exert a biological effect on prostate cells, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic potential.",
